@startuml BrowserViewport
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: trace browser requests between the operator, the agent and guest Chromium
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/browser.go
' covers: internal/guestbrowser/**
' covers: cmd/proveo-entrypoint/browser.go
' covers: e2e/browser_viewport_test.go
' profile lifecycle and verification: _spec/_plans/isolated-browser-profiles.puml
' explicit host browser: _spec/internal/sbx/host-browser-cdp.puml
title Isolated browser viewport

actor Operator as OP
participant "proveo\n127.0.0.1:<ephemeral>" as HOST
participant "sbx port@1\nlocalhost:<reported port>" as FWD
box "sbx guest" #F4F9FB
  participant "viewport\n:9222 · token required" as VIEW
  participant "agent CDP proxy\n127.0.0.1:9224" as CDP
  participant "Chromium\nloopback · kernel-selected port" as CHROME
  participant "agent-browser / Hermes" as AGENT
end box

HOST -> VIEW : verify this run's token via FWD
HOST --> OP : print a private loopback URL
OP -> HOST : open viewport
HOST -> FWD : authenticate viewport request
FWD -> VIEW : GET tabs
VIEW -> CHROME : start on first use and list CDP targets
AGENT -> CDP : discover and attach
CDP -> CHROME : start if needed and relay CDP
OP -> VIEW : take control via HOST and FWD
VIEW -> CDP : close admission and wait for pending replies
VIEW -> CHROME : capture tabs and dispatch operator input
OP -> VIEW : return control
VIEW -> CDP : admit new agent commands
HOST -> VIEW : close run's exec input
VIEW -> CHROME : Browser.close and wait for profile flush

note over HOST, FWD
  The viewport uses sbx's actual running publication. A randomly
  generated bearer authenticates the relay. The host proxy holds it
  and serves a run-scoped path with a loopback Host and Origin check.
  Before first use, the authenticated readiness probe checks only
  the launcher. The first viewport or agent request connects to CDP.
end note

note over VIEW, CDP
  The operator chooses a tab, including popups, and monitors its
  screenshot. Input needs an active control lease, which expires
  when its viewport stops checking in. Agent CDP commands get a
  retriable error during the operator lease. The boundary covers
  proxied CDP commands. Page scripts and network requests can
  continue after Chromium has acknowledged the initiating command.
end note

note over CHROME
  Chromium listens on guest loopback and uses the sandbox's egress.
  Browser profiles stay outside workspace and home synchronization.
  The guest has full CDP authority over its own browser.
end note
@enduml
